# ===========================================================================
# INTERNAL FILES — NEVER PUBLICLY SERVED
#
# Netlify publishes the repo root, so anything committed here is served. On
# 2026-07-20 /CLAUDE.md and /VOICE.md were both verified live over HTTP,
# returning the manifesto and the complete 640-line style bible as
# text/markdown. 43 internal audit .txt reports were served as text/plain.
#
# THE TRAILING "!" IS LOAD-BEARING. Netlify redirect rules are SHADOWED by
# real files: if a file exists at the requested path, Netlify serves the file
# and IGNORES the rule unless the status code is FORCED. An un-forced block
# was shipped first, reported as fixed, and did nothing at all. Never assert
# a redirect fix without re-fetching the live URL.
#
# THIS LIST IS ENFORCED, NOT REMEMBERED. validate-site.js CHECK 7 derives the
# runtime allowlist from the actual <script src> tags in the HTML and fails if
# any internal root file lacks a rule here. Add a build script or a working
# doc without a rule and the validator tells you. Preferred alternative for
# new working documents: put them in archive/ (CLAUDE.md INTEGRITY LAW 6),
# covered forever by the single forced splat below.
#
# Public by design and deliberately absent: robots.txt, the site-verification
# token, tags.json (fetched at runtime), the 11 front-end scripts, and every
# PDF under /Reformed Sources/.
# ===========================================================================

